From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@tuta.io>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:39:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: camss: Validate contiguous DMA ranges for capture

CAMSS uses the videobuf2 scatter-gather allocator but programs a DMA
base address for each plane. Reading the first mapped entry alone does
not ensure that the bytes the hardware will capture are addressable
from that base.

Use the common VB2 DMA prefix helper to require a mapping covering sizeimage
before saving an address. Accept adjacent DMA segments and ignore the
unused tail of a larger buffer. Fail in buf_init() so videobuf2 can
release the mapping without giving it to the hardware.

OpenAI Codex assisted with the source review and implementation.

Fixes: 0ac2586c410f ("media: camss: Add files which handle the video device nodes")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: slwyts <slwyts@tuta.io>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c
index 1b369fa584a7cebabe80e8b03a3c654f32c1f6bd..40869468e1adbffa76f8cc9ab04aed56a7694fc7 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 #include <media/v4l2-ioctl.h>
 #include <media/v4l2-mc.h>
 #include <media/videobuf2-dma-sg.h>
+#include <media/videobuf2-memops.h>
 
 #include "camss-video.h"
 #include "camss.h"
@@ -164,8 +165,10 @@ static int video_buf_init(struct vb2_buffer *vb)
 	unsigned int i;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < format->num_planes; i++) {
+		unsigned int size = format->plane_fmt[i].sizeimage;
+
 		sgt = vb2_dma_sg_plane_desc(vb, i);
-		if (!sgt)
+		if (!size || vb2_dma_contiguous_prefix(sgt, size) < size)
 			return -EFAULT;
 
 		buffer->addr[i] = sg_dma_address(sgt->sgl);
